  <div class="deck">
    <section class="slide active">
      <div class="kicker">ALFWorld · arXiv:2504.03553</div>
      <h1>KnowSelf: Teaching LLM Agents When to Think, Reflect, or Seek Knowledge</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Agentic knowledgeable self-awareness: a framework that lets LLM agents adaptively choose fast execution, reflective correction, or external knowledge retrieval based on task situation.</p>
      <div class="footer-note">Audience: ML researchers and graduate students in planning and agent systems</div>
      <div class="nav">1 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>Current Agent Training Uses “Flood Irrigation”</h2>
      <div class="grid-2" style="max-height:min(76vh,620px)">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Problem in Existing Paradigms</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Trajectory imitation injects full demonstrations regardless of need.</li>
            <li>Trial-and-error approaches add reflection everywhere, not selectively.</li>
            <li>Knowledge-augmented methods query knowledge in all steps (Know%=100%).</li>
            <li>Result: unnecessary context, higher compute, and potential action noise.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Why This Fails</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Different states require different cognition budgets.</li>
            <li>Humans switch between intuitive, deliberative, and knowledge-seeking modes.</li>
            <li>Agents lacking metacognitive routing overuse expensive modules.</li>
            <li>Goal: situationally decide <span class="highlight">when not</span> to retrieve knowledge.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">Core thesis: indiscriminate knowledge injection is both wasteful and suboptimal.</div>
      <div class="nav">2 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>Three Situational Modes: Decision Tree for Agent Cognition</h2>
      <div class="flow" style="max-height:min(74vh,610px)">
        <div class="mode">
          <h3>Fast Thinking</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Criterion: policy predicts correct next action directly.</li>
            <li>Behavior: execute immediately with minimal deliberation.</li>
            <li>Use case: routine state transitions and clear affordances.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="arrow">⟶</div>
        <div class="mode">
          <h3>Slow Thinking</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Criterion: initial action uncertain/incorrect but recoverable by reflection.</li>
            <li>Behavior: invoke self-reflection and revise action plan.</li>
            <li>Use case: ambiguity, long-horizon dependencies, planning slips.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:clamp(10px,1.2vh,16px)">
        <h3>Knowledgeable Thinking</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Criterion: environment state requires external facts not in parametric memory.</li>
          <li>Behavior: trigger retrieval/tool use, then continue planning with grounded evidence.</li>
          <li>Use case: commonsense/task priors (e.g., heating prerequisite, object placement rules).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">Special tokens supervise this routing decision during training and inference.</div>
      <div class="nav">3 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>KnowSelf Pipeline: Data Construction → Two-Stage Training → Self-Aware Inference</h2>
      <div class="pipeline" style="max-height:min(75vh,620px)">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">1</div>
          <h3>Heuristic Situation Judgment</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Self-explore trajectories on ALFWorld tasks.</li>
            <li>Label states as fast / slow / knowledgeable situations.</li>
            <li>Insert special cognitive-routing tokens into traces.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">2</div>
          <h3>Two-Stage Optimization</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Stage I: supervised fine-tuning on token-augmented traces.</li>
            <li>Stage II: RPO to reinforce decision quality and task success.</li>
            <li>No costly human dense annotations required.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">3</div>
          <h3>Self-Aware Inference</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Model emits situational token online at each step.</li>
            <li>Token gates direct action, reflection, or retrieval module.</li>
            <li>Achieves selective knowledge usage with higher final returns.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">Framework reference: figure_3.jpg in source brief.</div>
      <div class="nav">4 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>Qualitative Evidence: Reflection and Knowledge Triggers in Action</h2>
      <div class="grid-2" style="max-height:min(75vh,620px)">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Task A: “put a hot mug in cabinet”</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>KnowSelf detects planning mismatch and triggers slow-thinking reflection.</li>
            <li>Revised plan includes heating step before placement.</li>
            <li>Successfully completes sequence; baseline OpenAI-O1 fails this trajectory.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="metric">Signal: reflective correction of initially insufficient plan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Task B: “put a saltshaker in drawer”</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>KnowSelf identifies need for external procedural knowledge.</li>
            <li>Triggers knowledgeable-thinking path and retrieves task-relevant cue.</li>
            <li>Completes placement while DeepSeek-R1 becomes stuck.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="metric">Signal: retrieval only when endogenous policy is insufficient.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">Qualitative comparison source: figure_1.jpg in source brief.</div>
      <div class="nav">5 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>ALFWorld Results: KnowSelf Hits 84.33% with Only 15% Knowledge (Llama-8B)</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap" style="max-height:min(76vh,630px)">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Backbone</th><th>Method</th><th>Know%</th><th>pick&place</th><th>look_at_obj</th><th>pick_clean</th><th>pick_heat</th><th>pick_cool</th><th>pick_two</th><th>All</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td rowspan="6">GPT-4o</td><td>ReAct</td><td>0</td><td>88.52</td><td>67.39</td><td>58.10</td><td>69.44</td><td>33.82</td><td>49.25</td><td>76.12</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reflexion</td><td>0</td><td>89.34</td><td>64.34</td><td>58.57</td><td>66.22</td><td>30.88</td><td>51.49</td><td>73.73</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ExpeL</td><td>100</td><td>93.55</td><td>73.91</td><td>76.19</td><td>83.33</td><td>52.94</td><td>79.85</td><td>79.85</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ETO</td><td>0</td><td>86.89</td><td>64.78</td><td>60.48</td><td>69.28</td><td>35.29</td><td>50.75</td><td>74.48</td></tr>
            <tr><td>KnowAgent</td><td>100</td><td>90.98</td><td>65.65</td><td>67.86</td><td>77.03</td><td>51.47</td><td>68.66</td><td>77.61</td></tr>
            <tr><td>WKM</td><td>100</td><td>91.80</td><td>66.08</td><td>67.14</td><td>78.38</td><td>50.00</td><td>70.15</td><td>77.91</td></tr>
            <tr><td rowspan="2">Llama-8B</td><td>KnowSelf</td><td class="highlight">15</td><td class="highlight">95.08</td><td class="highlight">79.13</td><td class="highlight">81.90</td><td class="highlight">89.19</td><td class="highlight">57.35</td><td class="highlight">82.09</td><td class="highlight">84.33</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ExpeL</td><td>100</td><td>92.62</td><td>72.17</td><td>74.29</td><td>81.08</td><td>51.47</td><td>77.61</td><td>78.66</td></tr>
            <tr><td rowspan="2">Gemma-2B</td><td>KnowSelf</td><td class="highlight">26</td><td>93.55</td><td>73.91</td><td>76.19</td><td>83.33</td><td>52.94</td><td>79.85</td><td>79.85</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ExpeL</td><td>100</td><td>90.16</td><td>66.08</td><td>69.52</td><td>77.03</td><td>47.06</td><td>72.39</td><td>76.87</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="nav">6 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>Efficiency Advantage: 15–26% Knowledge Usage vs 100% Baselines</h2>
      <div class="chart" style="padding-bottom:clamp(52px,8vh,70px)">
        <div>
          <div class="bar" style="height:76.12%" data-label="GPT-4o ReAct\nKnow 0%"></div>
          <div class="metric">All: 76.12</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="bar" style="height:79.85%" data-label="GPT-4o ExpeL\nKnow 100%"></div>
          <div class="metric">All: 79.85</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="bar" style="height:77.91%" data-label="GPT-4o WKM\nKnow 100%"></div>
          <div class="metric">All: 77.91</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="bar knowself" style="height:84.33%" data-label="Llama-8B KnowSelf\nKnow 15%"></div>
          <div class="metric">All: 84.33</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="bar" style="height:78.66%" data-label="Llama-8B ExpeL\nKnow 100%"></div>
          <div class="metric">All: 78.66</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="bar knowself" style="height:79.85%" data-label="Gemma-2B KnowSelf\nKnow 26%"></div>
          <div class="metric">All: 79.85</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <ul>
          <li>KnowSelf attains highest accuracy while querying knowledge in only a minority of steps.</li>
          <li>Efficiency gain persists across model scales: Gemma-2B and Llama-8B both benefit.</li>
          <li>Empirical evidence supports selective retrieval over always-on retrieval.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="nav">7 / 8</div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
      <h2>Key Takeaways and Future Directions</h2>
      <div class="card" style="max-height:min(76vh,620px)">
        <ul>
          <li>Indiscriminate knowledge injection is wasteful and can reduce downstream performance.</li>
          <li>Special-token supervision enables practical situational self-awareness without heavy annotation.</li>
          <li>KnowSelf (Llama-8B) outperforms strong GPT-4o baselines: 84.33 vs 76.12 (ReAct), 79.85 (ExpeL).</li>
          <li>Only 15–26% knowledge usage is needed, versus 100% for full-knowledge methods.</li>
          <li>Framework generalizes across model scales: Gemma-2B KnowSelf reaches 79.85.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 style="margin-top:clamp(10px,1.2vh,16px)">Future Work</h3>
        <p>Extend self-aware routing to multi-agent coordination, continuous tool APIs, and adaptive confidence calibration under distribution shift.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">KnowSelf suggests metacognition is a first-class design axis for agent planners.</div>
      <div class="nav">8 / 8</div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const slides = [...document.querySelectorAll('.slide')];
    let idx = 0;
    function show(i) {
      idx = (i + slides.length) % slides.length;
      slides.forEach((s, j) => s.classList.toggle('active', j === idx));
    }
    addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (['ArrowRight','PageDown',' '].includes(e.key)) { e.preventDefault(); show(idx + 1); }
      if (['ArrowLeft','PageUp'].includes(e.key)) { e.preventDefault(); show(idx - 1); }
      if (e.key === 'Home') show(0);
      if (e.key === 'End') show(slides.length - 1);
    });
    let touchX = null;
    addEventListener('touchstart', e => touchX = e.changedTouches[0].clientX, {passive:true});
    addEventListener('touchend', e => {
      if (touchX == null) return;
      const dx = e.changedTouches[0].clientX - touchX;
      if (Math.abs(dx) > 40) show(idx + (dx < 0 ? 1 : -1));
      touchX = null;
    }, {passive:true});
  </script>
</body>
</html>
