      <h2>Three Situational Modes: Decision Tree for Agent Cognition</h2>
      <div class="flow" style="max-height:min(74vh,610px)">
        <div class="mode">
          <h3>Fast Thinking</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Criterion: policy predicts correct next action directly.</li>
            <li>Behavior: execute immediately with minimal deliberation.</li>
            <li>Use case: routine state transitions and clear affordances.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="arrow">⟶</div>
        <div class="mode">
          <h3>Slow Thinking</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Criterion: initial action uncertain/incorrect but recoverable by reflection.</li>
            <li>Behavior: invoke self-reflection and revise action plan.</li>
            <li>Use case: ambiguity, long-horizon dependencies, planning slips.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:clamp(10px,1.2vh,16px)">
        <h3>Knowledgeable Thinking</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Criterion: environment state requires external facts not in parametric memory.</li>
          <li>Behavior: trigger retrieval/tool use, then continue planning with grounded evidence.</li>
          <li>Use case: commonsense/task priors (e.g., heating prerequisite, object placement rules).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">Special tokens supervise this routing decision during training and inference.</div>
      <div class="nav">3 / 8</div>
